      "message": "I don\u0027t think the follow-ups I squashed have any more information than the subject and the signed-off-by, unfortunately. Since they are just churning the code, I think copy/pasting them into this patch\u0027s description is pointless.\n\nHowever, this bit does seem important:\n\n\"For instance, the change from using namespaced cap checks to non-namespaced cap check feels a bit subtle and deserves some rational.\"\n\nI totally agree.. however, that seems to be introduced by the base patch \"ANDROID: net: Paranoid network.\" and I can\u0027t find an explanation for it. It also seems really wrong to me that this snippet is not wrapped with the same #ifdef as the other changes.\n\nI get the feeling this was originally coming in from the current_has_cap() -\u003e capable() reversion, I\u0027m sure older kernels didn\u0027t have network namespaces so maybe this was overlooked when it was cherry-picked in. For us, since we aren\u0027t using namespaces or network namespaces, they should be equivalent?",
